# {{name}}

A cluster node on [id_effect](https://github.com/Industrial/id_effect)'s process mesh (`id_effect_node`), generated by `id-effect new --template cluster`.

```sh
cargo test     # two nodes on an in-process fabric
cargo run      # this node runs a counter on a peer and calls it
```

- `src/lib.rs` — `Counter`, a process behavior (casts add, calls read); `node()`, a `Mesh` that can host it; `round_trip()`, a remote spawn + cast + call as one effect.
- `src/main.rs` — starts this node (`NODE_NAME`) and a peer, runs the round trip under `run_main`.
- `tests/mesh.rs` — remote calls between two nodes, a fault for an unknown node, the binary.

Remote requests are at-most-once and bounded by a timeout; a node's processes are addressed by `name@host`. The nodes here share a `MeshFabric` (one process). Across hosts, connect the meshes with `id_effect_kit::node::TcpTransport` sessions (cookie handshake) and find peers with `StaticDiscovery` / `DnsDiscovery`; see the id_effect_node docs.

## Run it elsewhere

- `docker compose up --build` — the image from `Dockerfile`.
- `.github/workflows/ci.yml` — fmt, clippy, test and a docker build on every push.
